2.15 Arithmetic application\par
\par
Question: Write a program that asks the user to enter two integers and displays their sum, product, difference and quotient.\par
\par
Complete Java program:\par
\par
import java.util.Scanner;\par
\par
public class Arithmetic \{\par
    public static void main(String[] args) \{\par
\par
        Scanner input = new Scanner(System.in);\par
\par
        int number1;\par
        int number2;\par
\par
        System.out.print("Enter first integer: ");\par
        number1 = input.nextInt();\par
\par
        System.out.print("Enter second integer: ");\par
        number2 = input.nextInt();\par
\par
        System.out.printf("Sum: %d%n", number1 + number2);\par
        System.out.printf("Product: %d%n", number1 * number2);\par
        System.out.printf("Difference: %d%n", number1 - number2);\par
\par
        if (number2 != 0) \{\par
            System.out.printf("Quotient: %d%n", number1 / number2);\par
        \} else \{\par
            System.out.println("Cannot divide by zero.");\par
        \}\par
\par
        input.close();\par
    \}\par
\}\par
\par
Example output:\par
\par
Enter first integer: 10\par
Enter second integer: 2\par
Sum: 12\par
Product: 20\par
Difference: 8\par
Quotient: 5\par
\par
Note: Because both inputs are integers, Java performs integer division. For example, 7 / 2 produces 3, not 3.5.\par
\par
