\par
Complete Java program:\par
\par
import java.util.Scanner;\par
\par
public class Numbers \{\par
    public static void main(String[] args) \{\par
\par
        Scanner input = new Scanner(System.in);\par
\par
        System.out.print("Enter first integer: ");\par
        int a = input.nextInt();\par
\par
        System.out.print("Enter second integer: ");\par
        int b = input.nextInt();\par
\par
        System.out.print("Enter third integer: ");\par
        int c = input.nextInt();\par
\par
        int sum = a + b + c;\par
        int average = sum / 3;\par
        int product = a * b * c;\par
\par
        int smallest = a;\par
        int largest = a;\par
\par
        if (b < smallest) \{\par
            smallest = b;\par
        \}\par
\par
        if (c < smallest) \{\par
            smallest = c;\par
        \}\par
\par
        if (b > largest) \{\par
            largest = b;\par
        \}\par
\par
        if (c > largest) \{\par
            largest = c;\par
        \}\par
\par
        System.out.printf("Sum: %d%n", sum);\par
        System.out.printf("Average: %d%n", average);\par
        System.out.printf("Product: %d%n", product);\par
        System.out.printf("Smallest: %d%n", smallest);\par
        System.out.printf("Largest: %d%n", largest);\par
\par
        input.close();\par
    \}\par
\}\par
\par
Example: If the user enters 2, 3 and 4, the output is:\par
