2.32 Negative, Positive and Zero Values\par
\par
Question: Write a program that inputs five numbers and determines the number of negative numbers, positive numbers and zeros entered.\par
\par
Answer\par
\par
import java.util.Scanner;\par
\par
public class CountNumbers \{\par
    public static void main(String[] args) \{\par
\par
        Scanner input = new Scanner(System.in);\par
\par
        int positive = 0;\par
        int negative = 0;\par
        int zero = 0;\par
\par
        System.out.print("Enter first number: ");\par
        int a = input.nextInt();\par
\par
        System.out.print("Enter second number: ");\par
        int b = input.nextInt();\par
\par
        System.out.print("Enter third number: ");\par
        int c = input.nextInt();\par
\par
        System.out.print("Enter fourth number: ");\par
        int d = input.nextInt();\par
\par
        System.out.print("Enter fifth number: ");\par
        int e = input.nextInt();\par
\par
        if (a > 0) positive++;\par
        else if (a < 0) negative++;\par
        else zero++;\par
\par
        if (b > 0) positive++;\par
        else if (b < 0) negative++;\par
        else zero++;\par
\par
        if (c > 0) positive++;\par
        else if (c < 0) negative++;\par
        else zero++;\par
\par
        if (d > 0) positive++;\par
        else if (d < 0) negative++;\par
        else zero++;\par
\par
        if (e > 0) positive++;\par
        else if (e < 0) negative++;\par
        else zero++;\par
\par
        System.out.printf("Positive numbers: %d%n", positive);\par
        System.out.printf("Negative numbers: %d%n", negative);\par
        System.out.printf("Zeros: %d%n", zero);\par
\par
        input.close();\par
    \}\par
\}\par
\par
Example output\par
\par
Suppose the user enters:\par
\par
5\par
-3\par
0\par
8\par
-2\par
\par
The result is:\par
\par
Positive numbers: 2\par
Negative numbers: 2\par
Zeros: 1\par
\par
Explanation:\par
\par
A number greater than zero is positive.\par
\par
A number less than zero is negative.\par
\par
A number equal to zero is counted as zero.\par
\par
positive++ increases the positive counter by one. The same principle applies to the other counters.\par
\par
