2.35 Car-Pool Savings Calculator\par
\par
Question: Create an application that calculates the daily cost of driving to work using:\par
\par
a) Total miles driven per day\par
b) Cost per gallon of gasoline\par
c) Average miles per gallon\par
d) Parking fees per day\par
e) Tolls per day\par
\par
Answer\par
\par
import java.util.Scanner;\par
\par
public class CarPoolSavings \{\par
    public static void main(String[] args) \{\par
\par
        Scanner input = new Scanner(System.in);\par
\par
        System.out.print("Enter total miles driven per day: ");\par
        double miles = input.nextDouble();\par
\par
        System.out.print("Enter cost per gallon of gasoline: ");\par
        double gasPrice = input.nextDouble();\par
\par
        System.out.print("Enter average miles per gallon: ");\par
        double milesPerGallon = input.nextDouble();\par
\par
        System.out.print("Enter parking fees per day: ");\par
        double parking = input.nextDouble();\par
\par
        System.out.print("Enter tolls per day: ");\par
        double tolls = input.nextDouble();\par
\par
        if (miles < 0 || gasPrice < 0 ||\par
            milesPerGallon <= 0 || parking < 0 || tolls < 0) \{\par
\par
            System.out.println("Please enter valid values.");\par
\par
        \} else \{\par
            double fuelCost = (miles / milesPerGallon) * gasPrice;\par
\par
            double totalCost = fuelCost + parking + tolls;\par
\par
            System.out.printf("Daily fuel cost: %.2f%n", fuelCost);\par
            System.out.printf("Total daily driving cost: %.2f%n",\par
                    totalCost);\par
        \}\par
\par
        input.close();\par
    \}\par
\}\par
\par
Example output\par
\par
Suppose the user enters:\par
\par
Enter total miles driven per day: 40\par
Enter cost per gallon of gasoline: 4\par
Enter average miles per gallon: 20\par
Enter parking fees per day: 5\par
Enter tolls per day: 2\par
\par
The result is:\par
\par
Daily fuel cost: 8.00\par
Total daily driving cost: 15.00\par
\par
Explanation:\par
\par
First, calculate the fuel cost:\par
\par
\\[\par
\\text\{Fuel cost\} =\par
\\frac\{\\text\{Miles driven per day\}\}\{\\text\{Miles per gallon\}\}\par
\\times \\text\{Cost per gallon\}\par
\\]\par
\par
Using the example:\par
\par
\\[\par
\\frac\{40\}\{20\} \\times 4 = 8\par
\\]\par
\par
Then add the parking fees and tolls:\par
\par
\\[\par
8 + 5 + 2 = 15\par
\\]\par
\par
The total daily driving cost is 15 monetary units in this example.\par
\par
To estimate savings from carpooling, you could compare this cost with the amount you would personally pay when sharing a ride.\par
}
